<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">György Dózsa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1470–1514</span> · Also known as George Dózsa</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">György Dózsa was a Székely soldier from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transylvania">Transylvania</a> chosen to lead a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">crusade</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> proclaimed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> in 1514. The mostly peasant army turned against the nobility instead, and the revolt spread across the kingdom before it was crushed near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timisoara">Temesvár</a>. Dózsa was executed on a heated iron throne, and the diet then bound the peasants permanently to the land.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gyorgy-dozsa.jpg" alt="György Dózsa" width="320" height="401" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Viktor Madarász · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:D%C3%B3zsa_Gy%C3%B6rgy.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
